Description: GHSA-www2-q4fc-65wf: checkdnsrr(), dns_check_record(), dns_get_record(), dns_get_mx(), getmxrr(), inet_pton(), ip2long(), getservbyname(), getservbyport() and getprotobyname() refuse an argument with a NUL byte (a warning and NULL, as a path with one) instead of using the part before it; their warning for an argument of the wrong type says "a valid path" instead of "string", as in 7.4.
Origin: php-src commit 3e9d47f6cc04 (06.09.2025, Niels Dossche) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports), with its test; the variation tests of 5.6 (7.4 has none of them) expect the new warning

